= The Game Lobby

The *FujiNet Game Lobby* is a list of every network game that has a table open
right now, on every kind of computer and console FujiNet works with. Pick a
table and the Lobby loads the right game for your 5200 and sends you straight
to it.

To open the Lobby, move the bar to *PLAY GAME LOBBY* on HOST SLOTS and press
the bottom button (or #HASH). FujiNet finds the Lobby’s host,
*ec.tnfs.io*, and loads the Lobby from it:

- #scr("FINDING LOBBY HOST...") -- FujiNet looks for ec.tnfs.io among your
  hosts.
- #scr("ADDING LOBBY HOST...") -- if it is not there, FujiNet puts it in the
  first #scr("(EMPTY)") host. If all eight are full, it uses the eighth.
- Then *LOADING*, titled #scr("GAME LOBBY"), as for any game (Section 8).

#note[The Lobby for the 5200 is being finished now. Until it is ready, load
the network games from the browser, as Section 8 shows: each has its own
