== Your Name

FujiNet keeps one player name for all of its network games, so you type it
once. The first FujiNet game you play asks for it, and every game after that
-- on this console, and through the Lobby -- uses the same one. Names are up to
eight letters and numbers. 5 Card Stud, Texas Hold’em and Battleship change it
with #kp(4) at their table lists.

== Tables

The games’ servers keep several tables open all the time. The *AI Rooms* seat
you with robot players, which is the best way to learn a game; the others are
for people, from wherever they are playing -- on a 5200, an Atari computer, an
Apple, a PC or anything else FujiNet plugs into.
